1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,969
The Volk'ar: an alien hunter, cloaked and invisible, stalking the jungle.

2
00:00:04,189 --> 00:00:05,491
Here's how she plays.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:10,467
Add the two Track cards to your Action Tableau, and put the Attack Resolution card

4
00:00:10,467 --> 00:00:11,889
and tokens beside the board.

5
00:00:12,109 --> 00:00:14,861
Shuffle the Movement deck and deal one card face down.

6
00:00:15,081 --> 00:00:18,324
Her meeple doesn't go on the board. It sits on the Finale card.

7
00:00:18,544 --> 00:00:20,714
One Origin marker goes where she'd start;

8
00:00:20,714 --> 00:00:22,725
the other goes on that face-down card.

9
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:27,928
The Volk'ar has no Movement Value. She moves only by her Path of Movement cards.

10
00:00:28,148 --> 00:00:31,479
She is always in one of two states. Concealed means her cloak is on:

11
00:00:31,479 --> 00:00:35,495
she is always somewhere on the board, but you can't see where, and her meeple sits

12
00:00:35,495 --> 00:00:36,425
on the Finale card.

13
00:00:36,645 --> 00:00:40,703
Visible means the cloak is off: her meeple is on the board and she behaves like any

14
00:00:40,703 --> 00:00:41,339
other killer.

15
00:00:41,559 --> 00:00:44,156
At the start of each Killer phase, check her state.

16
00:00:44,156 --> 00:00:48,026
If she's Concealed, resolve the upper Killer Action line on her Finale card.

17
00:00:48,026 --> 00:00:50,113
If she's Visible, resolve the lower line.

18
00:00:50,933 --> 00:00:54,667
Her hidden route is the Path: a row of Movement cards, read left to right.

19
00:00:54,887 --> 00:00:59,233
The first card is the Origin card. One Origin marker sits on it, and the other sits

20
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:02,375
on the board, on the space where her hidden movement starts.

21
00:01:02,595 --> 00:01:06,888
Whenever you see the open eye icon, draw a Movement card and add it face up to the

22
00:01:06,888 --> 00:01:11,128
end of the Path. Whenever you see the crossed-out eye, add one face down instead.

23
00:01:11,348 --> 00:01:14,612
If the Movement deck runs out, shuffle the discards to make a new one.

24
00:01:14,612 --> 00:01:17,876
But you're never allowed to look through the discarded Movement cards.

25
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:22,241
If a crossed-out eye comes up while she's Visible, she vanishes straight away.

26
00:01:22,461 --> 00:01:26,734
The card you just drew face down becomes the new Origin card, with an Origin marker

27
00:01:26,734 --> 00:01:30,956
on it. The other Origin marker goes on the space she's standing in, and her meeple

28
00:01:30,956 --> 00:01:32,552
goes back onto the Finale card.

29
00:01:32,772 --> 00:01:36,271
From then on, every card added to the Path is another step you can't see.

30
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:40,663
Her Path is resolved, and she reveals herself, when one of three things happens.

31
00:01:40,883 --> 00:01:43,121
One: you resolve the Reveal icon on a card.

32
00:01:43,121 --> 00:01:45,620
Two: a sixth Movement card is added to the Path.

33
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:49,160
Three: while she's Concealed, an attack against her would do damage.

34
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:53,690
If the sixth card arrives part-way through her Finale Killer Action, or a Terror

35
00:01:53,690 --> 00:01:56,815
card, finish that whole card first, then resolve the Path.

36
00:01:56,815 --> 00:01:58,916
So her Path can end up longer than six.

37
00:01:59,733 --> 00:02:03,853
To resolve the Path, put her meeple on the space with the Origin marker, even if

38
00:02:03,853 --> 00:02:06,221
that space can't normally be entered any more.

39
00:02:06,221 --> 00:02:08,075
Put both Origin markers by the deck.

40
00:02:08,295 --> 00:02:12,330
Then work through the cards one at a time, starting with the Origin card, flipping

41
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:13,265
any face-down ones.

42
00:02:13,485 --> 00:02:18,048
Each card moves her: for example, three spaces towards the closest search space, or

43
00:02:18,048 --> 00:02:22,445
one space on a roll of six. The card says how to break ties, and some say not to

44
00:02:22,445 --> 00:02:24,259
count the space she's already in.

45
00:02:24,479 --> 00:02:28,812
If a card has a Killer Action line, she attacks in the space she ends that card in:

46
00:02:28,812 --> 00:02:33,145
Victims, Soldiers, or you. Location rules that stop or slow the Killer apply to her

47
00:02:33,145 --> 00:02:34,868
too, so sometimes she won't move.

48
00:02:35,088 --> 00:02:39,423
If anyone's Final Health token needs revealing, wait until every card is done.

49
00:02:39,423 --> 00:02:41,701
Then discard the Path. She's now Visible.

50
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:45,563
Use the Track action card to flip her Movement cards face up.

51
00:02:45,783 --> 00:02:49,579
With your best result you reveal the Origin card, or any two other cards.

52
00:02:49,579 --> 00:02:53,688
The middle result reveals two cards, and the lowest reveals one, but neither of

53
00:02:53,688 --> 00:02:55,404
those can reveal the Origin card.

54
00:02:55,624 --> 00:02:59,741
Revealing the Origin card matters most, because it tells you where her route begins.

55
00:02:59,961 --> 00:03:04,024
If every card in the Path is face up, you know exactly which space she's in, and you

56
00:03:04,024 --> 00:03:07,748
can follow her route on the board. If even one is face down, you're guessing.

57
00:03:08,567 --> 00:03:12,536
While she's Concealed you can attack any space in range, following the normal attack

58
00:03:12,536 --> 00:03:14,284
rules, as if she were standing there.

59
00:03:14,504 --> 00:03:18,636
Put the Attack token in that space and resolve the attack, placing the damage you

60
00:03:18,636 --> 00:03:21,288
roll as Damage tokens on the Attack Resolution card.

61
00:03:21,508 --> 00:03:23,872
If the attack did no damage, nothing happens:

62
00:03:23,872 --> 00:03:26,393
she stays Concealed and her Path isn't resolved.

63
00:03:26,613 --> 00:03:30,048
If it did any damage, resolve her whole Path now, card by card.

64
00:03:30,867 --> 00:03:34,666
If her final space is the one with the Attack token, your damage lands.

65
00:03:34,666 --> 00:03:37,288
Move it from the Attack Resolution card onto her.

66
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:41,635
If she ends anywhere else, the attack is wasted, and she ambushes you, even if the

67
00:03:41,635 --> 00:03:45,863
attack came from your Soldiers. Resolve the Ambush Penalty at the bottom of the last

68
00:03:45,863 --> 00:03:47,172
Movement card in her Path.

69
00:03:47,392 --> 00:03:50,741
Either way, clear the Damage tokens and the Attack token afterwards.

70
00:03:50,961 --> 00:03:54,963
One special case: if you attacked your own space, she ends there, and the last card

71
00:03:54,963 --> 00:03:58,385
has a Killer Attack line, your attack and hers happen at the same time.

72
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,483
While she's Concealed, a few other rules change.

73
00:04:01,703 --> 00:04:05,805
If an effect places something, or counts spaces, relative to the Killer, use the

74
00:04:05,805 --> 00:04:07,292
space with the Origin marker.

75
00:04:07,512 --> 00:04:10,019
If an effect says to place the Killer, ignore it.

76
00:04:10,019 --> 00:04:14,267
If any card has a Killer Action line, treat it as a crossed-out eye instead, adding

77
00:04:14,267 --> 00:04:15,597
a hidden card to her Path.

78
00:04:15,817 --> 00:04:18,271
And Victims don't panic during the Panic phase.

79
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:21,443
Watch for her Dark Powers. Blades in the Dark:

80
00:04:21,443 --> 00:04:25,672
whenever her Path is resolved, she kills one Victim in each space next to where she

81
00:04:25,672 --> 00:04:25,927
ends.

82
00:04:26,147 --> 00:04:30,851
Her Epic Dark Power, Merciless Ambush: whenever her Path is resolved, you suffer the

83
00:04:30,851 --> 00:04:35,163
Ambush Penalty on every Movement card in it, so long hidden Paths become very

84
00:04:35,163 --> 00:04:35,555
costly.

85
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:39,892
And her Psy Ops Terror card makes you discard every Track card in your hand if she's

86
00:04:39,892 --> 00:04:40,383
Concealed.

87
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:44,417
A few tips. Use Track to flip cards before a blind attack:

88
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:46,469
every face-up card narrows the guess.

89
00:04:46,689 --> 00:04:49,356
Strike while the Path is short, when she can't have gone far.

90
00:04:49,576 --> 00:04:53,405
She's very beatable: about three wins in four on Final Girl Stats.

91
00:04:53,405 --> 00:04:55,784
But Self Destruct is her toughest Finale.

92
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,116
Keep the rule sheet handy, and good hunting.

